     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">sean.or...@gmail.com</a> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">sean.or...@gmail.com</a>] <b>On Behalf Of </b>Sean O&#39;Riordain<br><b>Sent:</b> Tuesday, November 05, 2013 1:19 PM<br><b>To:</b> Roman Luštrik<br><b>Cc:</b> Trinh Quoc Trong Gmail; ggplot2<br><b>Subject:</b> Re: Multiple distributions<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">or perhaps<br><br>library(ggplot2)<br><br># dtot &lt;- function(x) dnorm(x, mean=180, sd=10)<br><br>dAa &lt;- function(x) dnorm(x, mean=185, sd=10)<br>dAA &lt;- function(x) dnorm(x, mean=210, sd=22)<br>daa &lt;- function(x) dnorm(x, mean=160, sd=15)<br>DTOT &lt;- function(x) daa(x) + dAa(x) + dAA(x)<br><br>qplot(1, xlab=&#39;Weight&#39;, ylab=&#39;Frequency&#39;, xlim=c(80,280), binwidth=1) +<br>  stat_function(fun=daa, color=&#39;blue&#39;) +<br>  stat_function(fun=DTOT, color=&#39;black&#39;) +<br>  stat_function(fun=dAa, color=&#39;red&#39;) +<br>  stat_function(fun=dAA, color=&#39;purple&#39;) +<br>  geom_vline(aes(xintercept=200), color=&#39;green&#39;)<br><br><br>cheers,<br>Sean<u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">On 5 November 2013 03:02, Roman Luštrik &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">roman....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Something like this? <a href=\"http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/stat_density.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-safered